verses.commentary:
3:11 This is a shocking statement. Judah had more spiritual light and opportunities than did
the northern tribes, but she did not learn from YHWH's judgment on them (cf. Ezek. 16:44-52; 23; Luke 12:48).

Israel is "faithless" (BDB 1000, cf. Jer. 3:6,8,12; also note Jer. 2:19; 3:22; 5:6; 8:5;
14:7) but Judah is "treacherous" (BDB 93, KB 108, Qal ACTIVE PARTICIPLE, cf. Jer. 3:8,20;
5:11; 12:6; Isa. 21:2; 24:16; 33:1). Both Hebrew roots denote a maintained apostasy. But, Judah had light and
was, therefore, more responsible.
